# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, a checkout on Windows with core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# every shell script to CRLF. That is harmless for scripts run on the host and
# fatal for one that is COPYd into an image: the shebang becomes "#!/bin/sh\r",
# the kernel looks for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", and the
# container dies at startup with
#
#     exec /docker-entrypoint-lolsuit.sh: no such file or directory
#
# which names the script rather than the interpreter and so reads like a
# missing file. client/docker-entrypoint.sh is the one that runs in a
# container, but every .sh here ends up on Linux sooner or later.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
